wmtube (0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Put ~/.local/bin first in $PATH at startup, so a pipx yt-dlp is found
    even when the window manager was started without it.
  * yt-dlp errors that usually mean yt-dlp is out of date end with
    "- TRY PIPX UPGRADE YT-DLP" on the tile, and no longer show part of
    yt-dlp's bug-report URL instead of the reason.
  * Suggest yt-dlp instead of recommending it: Debian's copy is usually
    too old for YouTube; install a current one with pipx.
  * Troubleshooting section in the man page; README says to install the
    package with apt rather than dpkg -i.

 -- Michael Sternberg <mhsternberg@gmail.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 20:36:07 -0500

wmtube (0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Playlists: Ctrl+left / Ctrl+right for previous / next track, and a
    -tracknum option that shows the position as TITLE [M/N].
  * Ctrl+Shift+left stops playback and resets to the startup state.
  * The idle tile starts quietly as WMTUBE; left click shows the help.
  * Internet radio / live streams: show elapsed time only, and clear the
    previous video's picture when switching to an audio-only stream.
  * Man page and README describe YouTube Music playlists and internet
    radio.

 -- Michael Sternberg <mhsternberg@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 20:49:12 -0500

